  "notes": "Half-time trap grid played loose: the pocket is elastic Thug-school rather than gridded, so the snare on 3 sits a few milliseconds late and the whole kit is quantized well under trap. The harmony is the marker — a two-chord loop of spacey Richie Souf keys that never resolves anywhere, with the vocal doing all the moving over it. Hence the wide melodic register, the constant octave jumps and the bluesy pentatonic colour: the record's variety is in the topline, not the changes. The 808 is warm and glides between roots instead of punching them.",
